//======================================================================================================================
// data/DefaultContent006-MashAndWaterProfiles.beer
//
// Example mash profiles.  They are locked (so they can be shared between recipes without being changed by accident) and
// they don't specify water amounts or temperatures, as these depend on the recipe.  The user adjusts these in the
// Mash Editor (which, for a locked mash, means making a copy for the recipe).
//
// Water profiles:
//   - Style target profiles, for use as the target profile on a recipe's Water tab (eg with Auto-Adjust).  These are
//     based on widely-published guidance (see the notes on each), and are ionically balanced so they can be made from
//     RO or distilled water with ordinary brewing salts.  (The classic historic city profiles -- Burton, Dortmund,
//     Dublin, etc -- are in DefaultContent001.)
//   - Starting profiles, ie the tap water of some well-known cities, from the water suppliers' own published figures
//     (see the notes on each for the source and date), for use as the base profile.
//
// Comments such as this one are part of the dotBeer format (which is JSON with comments allowed -- see "File format
// details" at https://github.com/Brewken/DotBeer), so software reading the file should be happy to import it.
//======================================================================================================================
