        "bicarbonate": {
          "unit": "ppm",
          "value": 0
        },
        "notes": "For light-coloured beers (about 2–5 SRM) with a malt-forward profile: low residual alkalinity and more chloride than sulfate.  Companion to the \"Light and hoppy\" profile.\n\nResidual alkalinity is about -46 ppm as CaCO₃."
      },
      {
        "name": "Pale, Soft (Pilsner, Helles)",
        "local_id": "water_target_02",
        "folder_path": "Target Profiles (Styles)",
        "calcium": {
          "unit": "ppm",
          "value": 50
        },
        "magnesium": {
          "unit": "ppm",
          "value": 5
        },
        "sodium": {
          "unit": "ppm",
          "value": 10
        },
        "chloride": {
          "unit": "ppm",
          "value": 65
        },
        "sulfate": {
          "unit": "ppm",
          "value": 65
        },
        "bicarbonate": {
          "unit": "ppm",
          "value": 15
        },
        "notes": "Soft water for delicate pale lagers such as Bohemian and German Pilsner, Helles and Kölsch, with just enough calcium for the yeast and an even sulfate to chloride balance.\n\nThis target profile is based on widely-published guidance: calcium of at least 50 ppm, sulfate to chloride ratio according to whether the beer is hoppy, balanced or malty, and bicarbonate (ie residual alkalinity) increasing with colour, to balance the acidity of darker malts.  The cations and anions balance (to within 3%), and there is enough sodium for the bicarbonate to come from baking soda, so the profile can be made exactly from RO or distilled water with the salts Auto-Adjust uses (gypsum, calcium chloride, Epsom salt, magnesium chloride, table salt and baking soda).  If you use chalk or pickling lime for the bicarbonate instead, you will end up with less sodium and more calcium.  Residual alkalinity is about -26 ppm as CaCO₃.  Use the Auto-Adjust button on a recipe's Water tab to work out the salts (and, if you set a target mash pH, acid) needed."
      },
      {
        "name": "Pale, Balanced (Blonde, Kölsch, Wheat)",
